{:id "0022-polish-emphasis-contrast"
 :title "People pick the stressed words, and quiet lines stay legible"
 :lupa/deps #{"0019-composer-delivery" "0020-credits-roll"}
 :lupa/area :flair
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "Two things from the foreman's first live conversation. (1) A
        headline sent by a person stressed 'engineer' because it was the
        longest word; people should choose. Words wrapped in *asterisks* in
        the composer become the message's emphasis, and the asterisks are
        removed from the sent text. (2) An aside's settled text looked
        faint; every effect's final state must meet 4.5:1 contrast."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/app/core.cljc" "test/halfahead/app/core_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/app/compose.cljc" "test/halfahead/app/compose_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/app/views.cljc" "test/halfahead/app/views_test.cljc"
         "public/css/halfahead.css"]
 :design "halfahead.app.compose (.cljc, pure):
            (parse-emphasis s) -> {:text t :emphasis spans}
            Each *run* (one or more non-asterisk characters between a pair
            of single asterisks, not starting or ending with whitespace)
            becomes a span over the run in t, with its asterisks removed.
            Unpaired asterisks, '**', and '* spaced *' stay literal. Only the
            first 8 runs become spans; any later run is left exactly as
            typed, asterisks included. If removing asterisks would leave
            t blank, return s unchanged with no emphasis.
          Core :composer/sent uses parse-emphasis on the trimmed text for
          every delivery (emphasis only changes how :headline performs);
          the resulting message must stay a valid :ha/message.
          Views: the Delivery group's 'headline' title attribute adds:
          'wrap the words to stress in *asterisks*'.
          CSS: the settled (--p 1) state of .fx-whisper, and of every other
          effect, meets 4.5:1 against the background in both colour
          schemes; list the pairs and ratios in a comment. Quietness comes
          from size and style, not from low contrast."
 :acceptance
 ["parse-emphasis: \"the *one* habit\" -> text \"the one habit\", emphasis
   [[4 7]]; \"*a* and *b c*\" -> two spans; \"2 * 3 * 4\" and \"**x**\" and
   \"* x *\" stay literal with no emphasis; \"**\" alone stays as is; nine
   marked words give 8 spans and the ninth keeps its asterisks (tests)"
  "Property: for any string, parse-emphasis returns spans that lie inside
   the returned text, are sorted and non-overlapping, at most 8"
  "Core: sending \"the *one* habit\" with delivery :headline emits a message
   with text \"the one habit\" and emphasis [[4 7]] (test)"
  "CSS comment lists each effect's settled foreground/background pair with
   its contrast ratio, all >= 4.5:1, in light and dark"
  "`bb test` stays green"]
 :non-goals
 ["No rich-text editor; no markdown beyond single-asterisk emphasis"
  "Do not edit the schema, perform, the shell, or the worker"
  "Do not run `bb e2e` or `bb play`"]
 :context ["src/halfahead/app/core.cljc" "src/halfahead/perform.cljc"
           "public/css/halfahead.css" "docs/SCHEMA.md" "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 8.0}
